Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:59:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 12/14] soc: qcom: add MSM8992 CPR open-loop voltages

Port of the open-loop part of the 3.10 kernel's cpr-regulator.c for
MSM8992: from the chip's fuses (speed bin, CPR fuse revision, ring
oscillator selects, per fuse corner init voltages) and the same qcom,cpr-*
properties, compute each virtual corner's voltage, interpolated down within
a fuse corner and limited to the floor/ceiling overrides, with the ceiling
reduced to it (qcom,cpr-scaled-init-voltage-as-ceiling).

The voltages go into the CPU OPP tables (dev_pm_opp_adjust_voltage); OPPs
above the speed bin are disabled. The MX corner is voted through
required-opps on the "mx" power domain. cpufreq-dt is started only after
every cluster has its voltages, so MSM8992 goes on the cpufreq-dt-platdev
blocklist.

Not ported: the closed loop, redundant fuse rows.
